Actual selected Skill loaded: No. The Codebase Investigator SKILL.md was not exposed as an accessible Skill resource in this session, so I did not claim to use it.

Cause: The cache is keyed only by id, but price() depends on both id and discount. After:

price("item", 0) // caches 100 under "item"

the second call finds "item" and returns the stale 100 instead of computing 80.

Minimal fix: Include discount in the cache key:

function price(id, discount) {
  const key = JSON.stringify([id, discount]);
  if (cache.has(key)) return cache.get(key);
  const result = 100 * (1 - discount);
  cache.set(key, result);
  return result;
}

Regression test:

expect(price("regression-item", 0)).toBe(100);
expect(price("regression-item", 0.2)).toBe(80);

This specifically fails with the original implementation because the second result would be 100.

